Zero OS 0.11 final optical boot regression

All four QEMU/TCG paths PASS: BIOS64, BIOS32 without long mode/PAE,
UEFI64 and UEFI32. The tested ISO is 18890752 bytes, SHA256
2c15dbc7e8f058c5ba07024c4c6c1ddd1ffcfcd86d15a2cc7c49ca7fbfd4a3df.

Tests used actual emulated PS/2 input and 1920x1080 framebuffers. They cover
automatic DHCP before input, cable loss/recovery, network progress while
computation is paused, real local HTTP packets and independent checksums,
keyboard apps, WiFi no-adapter state, terminal history, independent volume
roots, private ext4 reads, one-based tasks/pixels and compiler error recovery.
Public Internet reachability was not tested in this run. No physical WiFi
connection or native VirtualBox execution is implied.

New 0.11 checks execute the bundled Zero/Ezero tools on every architecture:
lines with CRLF/LF, empty input and trailing empty lines; nested lines/join;
joining a text list; numeric-element rejection with a line diagnostic;
successful compilation after the error; unavailable guest filesync/hostwait;
continued wired connection after compilation. All eight new checks passed
on each VM. Existing 0.10 application/host-fallback checks also passed and
their per-mode reports retain the explicit filename 0.10-extra.json.

All four machines were stopped. Original data.img/data.vdi and the canonical
ISO remained hash-identical. Every filesystem fixture was a private copy.
See results.json, matrix.json, per-mode 0.11-extra.json and action/serial logs.
The separate folder loader is tested in installer/boot/verification; its
no-CD-ROM test is not represented as one of these optical-boot runs.
